---
// Live demo for Baustein W2 "Tokenisierung im Modell", learning goal 1: a
// chat template turns several messages with roles into one single token
// sequence and adds text you never wrote. Edit a small chat and watch the
// sequence gpt-oss would get (real harmony template, real o200k_harmony
// tokenizer), drawn as the Baustein's freight train: ordinary wagons, marker
// wagons for special tokens. A shrunken context window shows the oldest
// messages dropping out first. Logic: src/scripts/demos/chat-sequence.js.
import Demo from './Demo.astro';
import { GOAL_WINDOW, START } from '../../scripts/demos/chat-sequence.js';

interface Props {
	lang: 'de' | 'en';
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const copy = {
	de: {
		title: 'Dein Chat als Tokenfolge',
		intro: 'Bearbeite den kleinen Chat aus Systemnachricht, Fragen und Antworten. Darunter siehst du sofort die eine lange Tokenfolge, die das Modell bekommt. Gebaut wird sie mit der echten Chat-Vorlage und dem echten Tokenizer von gpt-oss, nicht von Llama 3.1 wie im Text. Deshalb startet der Chat vom Anfang hier mit 86 statt 50 Tokens, deine Systemnachricht trägt die Rolle „developer“, und vor jeder Antwort steht eine zusätzliche Marke, die nur gpt-oss kennt.',
		note: 'Live im Browser: die offizielle Chat-Vorlage und der echte Tokenizer von gpt-oss-20b, geprüft gegen die Vorlage des Modells. Das Modell selbst rechnet hier nicht; die Antworten im Chat sind vorgegeben. Das Startbeispiel ergibt dieselben 86 Tokens wie im Diagramm mit den vier Vorlagen. Das Kontextfenster ist stark verkleinert, damit es mit ein paar Nachrichten voll wird; gpt-oss fasst 131.072 Tokens. Wie Anwendungen bei vollem Fenster Platz schaffen, ahmt die Demo vereinfacht nach; welche Nachricht sie opfert, siehst du am Regler. Tippst du selbst etwas wie <|end|>, bleibt es hier gewöhnlicher Text.',
		solution: 'Aus 86 werden 102 Tokens, obwohl „Und von Italien?“ nur ein paar Tokens hat. Die neue Frage bringt samt ihren Marken 8 Tokens, die Antwort „Paris.“ ebenfalls 8, und die 86 Tokens von vorher gehen komplett noch einmal mit. Die Vorlage baut bei jeder Nachricht den ganzen Zug neu, weil sich das Modell zwischen zwei Nachrichten nichts merkt. Bei jedem Chatbot wird deshalb jede Runde länger als die vorige und füllt das Kontextfenster weiter. Wie es sich füllt, zeigt die Aufschlüsselung mit dem verkleinerten Fenster.',
		chat: 'Der Chat',
		system: 'Systemnachricht (vom Anbieter der App)',
		user: 'Du',
		assistant: 'Assistent',
		add: 'Runde hinzufügen',
		remove: 'Letzte Runde entfernen',
		window: 'Kontextfenster (verkleinert)',
		train: 'Die Tokenfolge, die das Modell bekommt',
		legend: { special: 'Spezial-Tokens', added: 'von der Vorlage eingefügt', content: 'aus dem Chat' },
		loading: 'Tokenizer wird geladen …',
		goal: 'Vermute zuerst, um wie viele Tokens die Folge wächst, wenn du eine Runde hinzufügst: nur um die wenigen Tokens der neuen Frage „Und von Italien?“ oder um mehr. Dann füg die Runde hinzu.',
		more: 'Aufschlüsselung und Längengrenze (mehr dazu im Abschnitt über das Kontextfenster)',
		moreGoal: `Stell das Kontextfenster auf ${GOAL_WINDOW.de} Tokens: Welche Nachricht fällt als Erste heraus?`,
	},
	en: {
		title: 'Your chat as a token sequence',
		intro: 'Edit the small chat of system message, questions, and answers. Below, you see at once the one long token sequence the model gets. It is built with gpt-oss’s real chat template and real tokenizer, not Llama 3.1’s as in the text. That is why the chat from the beginning starts here with 84 tokens instead of 45, your system message has the role “developer”, and each answer is preceded by an extra marker that only gpt-oss knows.',
		note: 'Live in your browser: the official chat template and the real tokenizer of gpt-oss-20b, checked against the model’s template. The model itself does not compute here; the answers in the chat are given. The start example gives the same 84 tokens as the diagram of the four templates. The context window is shrunk drastically so a few messages fill it; gpt-oss holds 131,072 tokens. The demo imitates in a simplified way how applications make room when the window is full; the slider shows which message it sacrifices. If you type something like <|end|> yourself, it stays ordinary text here.',
		solution: 'The 84 tokens become 99, although “And Italy?” has only a few tokens. The new question brings 7 tokens with its markers, the answer “Paris.” brings 8, and the 84 tokens from before go along in full once more. The template rebuilds the whole train for every message, because the model remembers nothing between two messages. With every chatbot, each round is therefore longer than the one before and fills the context window further. How it fills up is shown by the breakdown with the shrunk window.',
		chat: 'The chat',
		system: 'System message (from the app’s provider)',
		user: 'You',
		assistant: 'Assistant',
		add: 'Add a round',
		remove: 'Remove last round',
		window: 'Context window (shrunk)',
		train: 'The token sequence the model gets',
		legend: { special: 'special tokens', added: 'inserted by the template', content: 'from the chat' },
		loading: 'Loading the tokenizer …',
		goal: 'First guess how many tokens the sequence grows by when you add a round: only by the few tokens of the new question “And Italy?” or by more. Then add the round.',
		more: 'Breakdown and length limit (more on this in the section on the context window)',
		moreGoal: `Set the context window to ${GOAL_WINDOW.en} tokens: which message drops out first?`,
	},
}[lang];
const uid = `chatseq-${lang}`;
const start = START[lang];
---

<Demo lang={lang} id={`chatsequence-${lang}`} title={copy.title} intro={copy.intro} note={copy.note} origin="tokenizer" solution={copy.solution}>
	<div
		class="cs"
		data-chatseq-demo
		data-lang={lang}
		data-user={copy.user}
		data-assistant={copy.assistant}
		data-testid="demo-chatsequence"
	>
		<p class="cs-goal" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-goal">{copy.goal}</p>

		<fieldset class="kev-demo-panel cs-chat" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-chat">
			<legend class="kev-demo-label">{copy.chat}</legend>
			<div class="cs-msg cs-msg--system">
				<label class="cs-role" for={`${uid}-system`}>{copy.system}</label>
				<textarea id={`${uid}-system`} class="cs-field" rows="1" maxlength="300" spellcheck="false" data-system data-testid="demo-chatsequence-system">{start.system}</textarea>
			</div>
			<div class="cs-messages" data-messages></div>
			<div class="kev-demo-actions">
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-add data-testid="demo-chatsequence-add-round">{copy.add}</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" data-remove data-testid="demo-chatsequence-remove-round">{copy.remove}</button>
			</div>
		</fieldset>

		<div class="cs-result" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-result">
			<p class="cs-count" aria-live="polite" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-count"><span data-count>{copy.loading}</span></p>
		</div>

		<div>
			<p class="kev-demo-label">{copy.train}</p>
			<div class="cs-train" data-train aria-hidden="true" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-train"></div>
		</div>

		<details class="cs-more" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-more">
			<summary data-testid="demo-chatsequence-more-toggle">{copy.more}</summary>
			<p class="cs-more-goal">{copy.moreGoal}</p>
			<ul class="cs-legend" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-legend">
				<li><span class="cs-swatch cs-k-special"></span>{copy.legend.special}: <strong data-n="special">…</strong></li>
				<li><span class="cs-swatch cs-k-added"></span>{copy.legend.added}: <strong data-n="added">…</strong></li>
				<li><span class="cs-swatch cs-k-content"></span>{copy.legend.content}: <strong data-n="content">…</strong></li>
			</ul>
			<div class="kev-demo-range">
				<label class="kev-demo-label" for={`${uid}-window`}>{copy.window}</label>
				<output for={`${uid}-window`} data-window-out data-testid="demo-chatsequence-window-value"></output>
				<input id={`${uid}-window`} type="range" min="40" max="300" step="1" value="160" data-window data-testid="demo-chatsequence-window" />
			</div>
			<div class="cs-budget" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="demo-chatsequence-budget">
				<span class="cs-budget-seg cs-k-special" data-seg="special"></span><span class="cs-budget-seg cs-k-added" data-seg="added"></span><span class="cs-budget-seg cs-k-content" data-seg="content"></span>
			</div>
			<p class="kev-demo-live" aria-live="polite" data-status data-testid="demo-chatsequence-status"></p>
		</details>
	</div>
</Demo>

<script>
	import { addRound, countKinds, encodeChat, fitWindow, removeRound, ROUNDS, START } from '../../scripts/demos/chat-sequence.js';
	import { displayToken, loadTokenizer } from '../../scripts/demos/real-tokens.js';

	type Lang = 'de' | 'en';
	type Chat = { system: string; messages: { role: 'user' | 'assistant'; content: string }[] };
	type Token = { id: number; text: string | null; bytes: number[] | null; kind: 'special' | 'added' | 'content' };
	type Block = { kind: string; role?: string; index?: number; tokens: Token[] };

	const TEXT = {
		de: {
			tokens: (n: number) => `${n.toLocaleString('de-DE')} Tokens`,
			window: (n: number) => `${n} Tokens`,
			ok: (used: number, free: number) => `${used} Tokens im Fenster, ${free} Tokens frei für die Antwort.`,
			dropped: (n: number, tokens: number, free: number) =>
				`Fenster voll: ${n === 1 ? 'Die älteste Nachricht fährt' : `Die ${n} ältesten Nachrichten fahren`} nicht mehr mit (${tokens} Tokens), so wie Anwendungen wie claude.ai alte Teile herausfallen lassen können. ${free} Tokens frei für die Antwort.`,
			tooLong: (used: number, size: number) => `Zu lang: Auch ohne Verlauf braucht die Anfrage ${used} Tokens, das Fenster fasst nur ${size}. Die Anfrage würde abgelehnt.`,
			failed: 'Der Tokenizer konnte nicht geladen werden.',
		},
		en: {
			tokens: (n: number) => `${n.toLocaleString('en-US')} tokens`,
			window: (n: number) => `${n} tokens`,
			ok: (used: number, free: number) => `${used} tokens in the window, ${free} tokens free for the answer.`,
			dropped: (n: number, tokens: number, free: number) =>
				`Window full: ${n === 1 ? 'the oldest message no longer rides' : `the ${n} oldest messages no longer ride`} along (${tokens} tokens), just as applications such as claude.ai can let old parts drop out. ${free} tokens free for the answer.`,
			tooLong: (used: number, size: number) => `Too long: even without the history, the request needs ${used} tokens; the window holds only ${size}. It would be rejected.`,
			failed: 'The tokenizer could not be loaded.',
		},
	};

	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-chatseq-demo]')) {
		const lang: Lang = root.dataset.lang === 'en' ? 'en' : 'de';
		const t = TEXT[lang];
		const roleName = { user: root.dataset.user ?? 'user', assistant: root.dataset.assistant ?? 'assistant' };
		const system = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('[data-system]')!;
		const list = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-messages]')!;
		const add = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-add]')!;
		const remove = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-remove]')!;
		const range = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-window]')!;
		const windowOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-window-out]')!;
		const count = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-count]')!;
		const status = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]')!;
		const train = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-train]')!;

		let chat: Chat = structuredClone(START[lang]) as Chat;
		let api: unknown = null;
		let blocks: Block[] = [];

		// Keep textareas as tall as their text (no inner scrollbars).
		const grow = (field: HTMLTextAreaElement) => {
			field.style.height = 'auto';
			field.style.height = `${field.scrollHeight + 2}px`;
		};

		const renderEditor = () => {
			const uid = `${system.id.replace(/-system$/, '')}-msg`;
			list.replaceChildren(
				...chat.messages.map((m, i) => {
					const row = document.createElement('div');
					row.className = `cs-msg cs-msg--${m.role}`;
					const label = document.createElement('label');
					label.className = 'cs-role';
					label.htmlFor = `${uid}-${i}`;
					label.textContent = roleName[m.role];
					const field = document.createElement('textarea');
					field.id = `${uid}-${i}`;
					field.className = 'cs-field';
					field.rows = 1;
					field.maxLength = 300;
					field.spellcheck = false;
					field.value = m.content;
					field.dataset.testid = `demo-chatsequence-message-${i}`;
					field.addEventListener('input', () => {
						chat.messages[i] = { ...chat.messages[i], content: field.value };
						grow(field);
						schedule();
					});
					row.append(label, field);
					return row;
				}),
			);
			list.querySelectorAll<HTMLTextAreaElement>('textarea').forEach(grow);
			add.disabled = chat.messages.length >= 1 + 2 * ROUNDS[lang].length;
			remove.disabled = chat.messages.length < 3;
		};

		const wagon = (token: Token) => {
			const el = document.createElement('span');
			el.className = `cs-wagon cs-k-${token.kind}`;
			el.textContent = token.kind === 'special' ? (token.text ?? '') : displayToken(token);
			el.title = `ID ${token.id}`;
			return el;
		};

		const renderTrain = () => {
			train.replaceChildren(
				...blocks.map((block) => {
					const group = document.createElement('span');
					group.className = 'cs-block';
					group.append(...block.tokens.map(wagon));
					return group;
				}),
			);
		};

		const renderWindow = () => {
			const size = Number(range.value);
			windowOut.textContent = t.window(size);
			if (!api) return;
			const fit = fitWindow(blocks, size);
			train.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.cs-block').forEach((el, i) => el.classList.toggle('is-out', fit.out[i]));
			const kinds = countKinds(blocks, fit.out);
			for (const kind of ['special', 'added', 'content'] as const) {
				root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-n="${kind}"]`)!.textContent = String(kinds[kind]);
				root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-seg="${kind}"]`)!.style.width = `${Math.min(100, (kinds[kind] / size) * 100)}%`;
			}
			root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.cs-budget')!.dataset.over = String(fit.tooLong);
			const droppedMessages = fit.out.filter(Boolean).length;
			if (fit.tooLong) {
				status.textContent = t.tooLong(fit.used, size);
				status.dataset.tone = 'warn';
			} else if (droppedMessages > 0) {
				status.textContent = t.dropped(droppedMessages, fit.dropped, fit.free);
				status.dataset.tone = 'amber';
			} else {
				status.textContent = t.ok(fit.used, fit.free);
				status.dataset.tone = '';
			}
		};

		const update = () => {
			if (!api) return;
			const before = blocks.reduce((n, b) => n + b.tokens.length, 0);
			blocks = encodeChat(api, chat) as Block[];
			const total = blocks.reduce((n, b) => n + b.tokens.length, 0);
			count.textContent = t.tokens(total);
			if (before && total !== before) {
				count.classList.remove('kev-demo-flash');
				void count.offsetWidth;
				count.classList.add('kev-demo-flash');
			}
			renderTrain();
			renderWindow();
		};

		let frame = 0;
		const schedule = () => {
			cancelAnimationFrame(frame);
			frame = requestAnimationFrame(update);
		};

		system.addEventListener('input', () => {
			chat.system = system.value;
			grow(system);
			schedule();
		});
		add.addEventListener('click', () => {
			chat = addRound(chat, lang) as Chat;
			renderEditor();
			update();
		});
		remove.addEventListener('click', () => {
			chat = removeRound(chat) as Chat;
			renderEditor();
			if (remove.disabled) add.focus();
			update();
		});
		range.addEventListener('input', renderWindow);

		renderEditor();
		grow(system);
		renderWindow();

		// The engine (~1 MB) loads only when the demo comes near the screen.
		let loading = false;
		const load = () => {
			if (loading) return;
			loading = true;
			loadTokenizer('o200k_harmony')
				.then((engine) => {
					api = engine.api;
					update();
				})
				.catch(() => {
					count.textContent = t.failed;
				});
		};
		const io = new IntersectionObserver(
			(entries) => {
				if (entries.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) {
					io.disconnect();
					load();
				}
			},
			{ rootMargin: '600px 0px' },
		);
		io.observe(root);
		root.addEventListener('focusin', load, { once: true });
	}
</script>

<style is:global>
	.cs {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--sp-md);
	}
	.cs-goal {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.cs-more {
		padding: var(--sp-sm) var(--sp-md);
		border: 1px solid var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-lg);
	}
	.cs-more[open] {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--sp-sm);
	}
	.cs-more > summary {
		cursor: pointer;
		font-weight: 650;
		color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.cs-more > summary:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid var(--focus);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
	.cs-more-goal {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.cs-chat {
		display: grid;
		gap: 10px;
		margin: 0;
		border: none;
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.cs-chat > legend {
		float: left;
		width: 100%;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.cs-messages {
		display: grid;
		gap: 10px;
	}
	.cs-msg {
		display: grid;
		gap: 4px;
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.cs-msg--assistant {
		padding-left: clamp(8px, 4vw, 32px);
	}
	.cs-role {
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	.cs-field {
		width: 100%;
		min-width: 0;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		resize: none;
		overflow: hidden;
		font: inherit;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.02rem;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--ink);
		padding: 8px 12px;
		background: var(--ground-page);
		border: 1.5px solid var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
	}
	.cs-msg--system .cs-field {
		border-style: dashed;
	}
	.cs-field:focus-visible {
		outline: none;
		border-color: var(--petrol-viv);
		box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(18, 144, 127, 0.2);
	}
	.cs-result {
		display: grid;
		gap: 10px;
		justify-items: start;
	}
	.cs-count {
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		line-height: 1.1;
		color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.cs-budget {
		display: flex;
		width: 100%;
		height: 14px;
		overflow: hidden;
		border: 1px solid var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-pill);
		background: var(--ground-page);
	}
	.cs-budget[data-over='true'] {
		border-color: var(--error);
	}
	.cs-budget-seg {
		display: block;
		height: 100%;
		transition: width 0.3s ease;
	}
	.cs-legend {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 4px 16px;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	.cs-legend li {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 6px;
	}
	.cs-legend strong {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.cs-swatch {
		width: 14px;
		height: 14px;
		border-radius: 3px;
		border: 1px solid var(--line-deep);
	}
	/* Token kinds: ordinary wagons (chat text), template wagons, marker wagons. */
	.cs-k-content {
		background: var(--demo-c1);
	}
	.cs-k-added {
		background: var(--demo-c3);
	}
	.cs-k-special {
		background: var(--demo-c2);
		border-color: var(--amber-viv);
	}
	.cs-train {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 4px 3px;
		padding: 10px;
		border: 1px dashed var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-lg);
		min-height: 3rem;
	}
	.cs-block {
		display: contents;
	}
	.cs-wagon {
		display: inline-block;
		max-width: 100%;
		overflow: hidden;
		text-overflow: ellipsis;
		white-space: pre;
		padding: 2px 5px;
		border: 1px solid transparent;
		border-radius: 4px;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		line-height: 1.35;
		color: var(--ink);
		transition: opacity 0.25s ease, filter 0.25s ease;
	}
	.cs-wagon.cs-k-special {
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--amber-deep);
	}
	.cs-block.is-out .cs-wagon {
		opacity: 0.35;
		filter: grayscale(1);
		border-style: dashed;
		border-color: var(--line-deep);
		text-decoration: line-through;
	}
</style>
